# The `files` allowlist in package.json decides what ships. This file exists
# mainly so npm does NOT fall back to .gitignore, whose `dist/` rule matches
# `app/dist/` and silently drops the built UI that `polygraph demo` serves.
#
# Everything below is belt-and-braces: already outside the allowlist, listed
# here so an accidental allowlist widening can't ship it.

.superpowers/
reference/
gates/
test/
src/
docs/
scripts/
fixture/
.claude/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.db
.env
Dockerfile
fly.toml
fleet.yaml
fleet.example.yaml
PROGRESS.md
CLAUDE.md
tsconfig*.json
vitest.config.ts
package-lock.json

# app/ ships only its built output (allowlisted as app/dist/); npm pulls in
# READMEs at any depth on its own, and the app's is internal notes.
app/README.md
